DESCRIPTION:Glickman building\, 9th floor. Check in at desk Q9.\n\n216.44
 4.5600 - procedure place.\n\n216.444.9239.  Anyone can assist.  Christin
 e.\n\nGetting Ready for the Test\n\n\n\n• You do not have to fast before
  the test.\n\n• Begin to drink 24-32 ounces of fluid (water\, cranberry 
 juice\, milk\, \nherbal tea) 90 minutes prior to the test so you arrive 
 at the Cleveland \nClinic with the urge to empty your bladder. You shoul
 d not be \nuncomfortable. If you have urinary urgency\, you may adjust t
 he amount of \nwater and the time that you drink the water to suit your 
 bladder.\n\n• Avoid drinks with caffeine on the day of your test (e.g. c
 offee\, tea and \ncolas).\n\n• Bathe or shower before your test.\n\n• A 
 woman’s menstrual cycle does not interfere with the test. You may wear \
 na tampon.\n\n• If you currently wear a pessary for pelvic organ prolaps
 e\, please wear \nit to your appointment.\n\n• You may find it more comf
 ortable if you have a bowel movement before the \ntest. This is not esse
 ntial.\n\n• Do not empty your bladder when you arrive at the Cleveland C
 linic.\n\n• Speak with a nurse if you feel you must empty your bladder.\
 n\n• If you are taking antibiotics for a urinary tract infection (UTI) o
 r \nbladder infection\, notify your physician’s office immediately. We m
 ay \nreschedule your bladder test.\n\n• Bring a list of all prescribed a
 nd over the counter medications you are \ntaking.\n\n• If you are taking
  overactive bladder medications like Detrol\, Ditropan\, \nVesicare\, En
 ablex\, Gelnique or Oxytrol\, Sanctura\, Myrbetriq\, Toviaz please \ndis
 continue for 3 days prior to testing.\n\n\n\nWhat Happens During the Tes
 t\n\n\n\n• You change into a hospital gown.\n\n• The nurse asks you abou
 t your symptoms and general health before \nstarting the test.\n\n• Ther
 e are three phases to the test.\n\n\n\nPhase 1\n\n\n\n• You are asked to
  urinate into a container. The container is joined to a \ncomputer that 
 records the speed and amount of urine you pass.\n\n\n\nPhase 2\n\n\n\n• 
 A small catheter is inserted into your bladder and another small \ncathe
 ter is inserted into your rectum or vagina.\n\n• Your bladder will be sl
 owly filled with sterile water and the nurse will \nask you a series of 
 questions while your bladder is being filled.\n\n• This part of the test
  shows what happens in the bladder as it fills. It \nmeasures the follow
 ing: how much pressure there is\; how much fluid you \nhold before you f
 eel full\; how much your bladder can hold\; and if you leak \nwhen you c
 ough or bear down.\n\n\n\nPhase 3\n\n\n\n• The catheter and rectal or va
 ginal catheter are removed when your test \nis finished.\n\n\n\nAfter th
 e Test\n\n\n\n• You may experience a slight burning and a small amount o
 f blood in your \nurine when you urinate. This should go away within 24-
 48 hours after your \ntest. Drink about 4-6 cups of fluid.\n\n• Avoid dr
 inks with caffeine or alcohol for 24 hours after your test.\n\n\n\n\n\nP
 lease be advised\, if you are not scheduled with your specific URO/GYN \
 nprovider for testing you will not have an appointment with a provider \
 nafter testing is complete. A follow up appointment will need to be \nsc
 heduled with your specific URO/GYN provider for your testing results.\n\
 nIf testing is scheduled with your specific URO/GYN provider\, you will 
 see \nyour provider after testing is completed to review results. 
